Imagine you're surrounded by nasties down to 5 hit points or less.
You've got stuff that can help you in a bag, but you'll never get to
it in time.  What now?

You read your scroll of repulsion.  

A wall of force springs up and pushes everyone back one square from
you. They can't reach you, you can't reach them.  They can still shoot
you or magic you (and vice versa) but you're safe from melee attack
for the moment.

The force field has a strength equal to XX hit points and AC 0. This
means that a low-level creature like a goblin can pound on it all day
and never break it, while against a Rider or a demon lord it would
last only a round or two.  But this should give you enough time to
pull out a potion, engrave the Word, or do something -- anything -- to
save your life.  In short, what it gives you is time.

If the creature is standing in front of a wall, it will be propelled
THROUGH the wall and take hit point damage from that, but the force
field will be in place.  If the wall is undiggable or otherwise
impossible to break, the force field will collapse but the creature
will take HP damage equal to the HP of the force field as it is rammed
against the wall with the message "The wall of force squishes the
<monster>!"  If more than 1 monster is so effected, the amount of
damage is divided among them equally.

If the monsters do not break the barrier, it will persist on its own
for XX turns and then dissolve, losing X hit points per turn until
gone.  It will remain centered on the character, moving where the
character moves.  Monsters will move back (or attack the field). The
character can force creatures into walls, inflicting X hit point
crushing damage on them -- but an equal amount of damage is inflicted
to the field.  Again, crushing more than 1 monster divides the damage
between them equally.

Objects on the ground are not affeted -- only monsters.  

A blessed scroll of repulsion will have increased HP, a decreased AC,
an increased timer, and a decreased loss of hp per turn active.

A cursed scroll will -- instead of repelling monsters -- repel the
character!  The character will be physically thrown 2 squares in a
random direction and take X hp damage when (s)he lands with a crunch
at the end of the trajectory.  If there is a wall in the way, the
character will be affected as a monster above -- either being
propelled through the wall or being crushed against it if it can't be
dug.

Estimated cost: 500-700 zorkmids.  

